course: dictionary
lesson: 7365
title: Please and pleased
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Please» is the small polite word you add when you ask for something: «Can I have some water, please?» It is one of the magic words, with «thank you». Saying please shows good manners, but it does not mean you will always get what you ask for.
explain: The word changes shape. To please someone means to make them happy: «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%.» Here pleased means happy about something. Read the clues around the word to choose its meaning.
explain: «Yes, please» is a polite way to accept something. «As you please» means whatever you want, as in «Stay or go, as you please.» When you meet a new use, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Please is a polite word, and it is one of the magic words with thank you.
fact: «Yes, please» is a polite way to accept an offer.
fact: To please someone means to make them happy or satisfied.
fact: «Pleased» means happy about something, as in «pleased to meet you».
fact: «As you please» or «whatever you please» means whatever you want.
exercise: «Can I have some water, please?» Why is please used here? | *It is a polite word that makes a request polite | It means you will pay for the water | It is a number | It means you have already got the water
exercise: «Teachers are pleased by a score of 100%.» What does pleased mean? | Sold out | Annoyed and cross | Very tired | *Happy about something
exercise: At the door, the host says «qǐng jìn», which means come in, please. What does it mean? | Go out | *Come in, please | Have some water | Sit down
test: «Stay or go, as you please.» What does as you please mean? | Without any money | *Whatever you want | Very quickly | Only if the teacher says so
test: To please someone means to | Make them cross | Hide from them | Lend them money | *Make them happy or satisfied
exam: Gran offers Sam a biscuit and Sam says «Yes, please». What does «Yes, please» show? | It means he is cross | It means no | *It is a polite way to accept | It is only for Mum to say
